<title>NEW ZEALAND: New Zealand ADRs mostly stronger as Dow rises.</title>
<headline>New Zealand ADRs mostly stronger as Dow rises.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were mostly stronger in late New York trade (7.50 a.m. NZT) as the Dow rose 18.83 points to 6,287.18.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company	Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$30 1/2	 +0 1/2 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$27 1/2	 +0 1/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 3/8	 nil *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$16 3/8	 +0 1/2 *</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$82 3/4	 nil *</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$17 1/8	 nil *</p>
<p>Thistle	  London  171 1/2	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  33		  -0 1/2</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  54		  +25.99</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  236 1/2	   -0 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  146 1/2	   -2 3/4</p>
<p>Templeton	London  132		 +1 1/4</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  A$3.00	     nil</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.54	     -3</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$2.93	     -2</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares. Evergreen is in bundles of 20.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
